  "name": "Total wealth",
  "unit": "$",
  "description": "Total wealth is calculated by summing up each component of wealth (“bottom-up approach”): Natural capital + Produced capital + Human capital + Net foreign assets. Each of these components is calculated separately by the World Bank, usually as the net present value of future returns. Data on each wealth component - i.e. market exchange rates - comes from various sources.",
